    {
      "_key": "en",
      "_type": "object",
      "value": [
        {
          "_key": "000000000001",
          "_type": "block",
          "children": [
            {
              "_key": "aer21nyh9cf0",
              "_type": "span",
              "marks": [],
              "text": "History Of "
            },
            {
              "_key": "caas1v0hwy6b",
              "_type": "span",
              "marks": [
                "0k2b399fqbk5"
              ],
              "text": "Al Wadi Al Gadid"
            }
          ],
          "markDefs": [
            {
              "_key": "0k2b399fqbk5",
              "_type": "internalLink",
              "reference": {
                "_ref": "wp-page-58952",
                "_type": "reference"
              }
            }
          ],
          "style": "h2"
        },
        {
          "_key": "000000000006",
          "_type": "block",
          "children": [
            {
              "_key": "e9hossyba0lo",
              "_type": "span",
              "marks": [],
              "text": "Al Wadi Al Gadid, a region steeped in the rich tapestry of Egyptian history, offers a unique window into the past through the "
            },
            {
              "_key": "60ehtp5rrw4k",
              "_type": "span",
              "marks": [
                "3eoenl5buc4c"
              ],
              "text": "El Wadi El Gedid museum"
            },
            {
              "_key": "1m6ehi1i2kul",
              "_type": "span",
              "marks": [],
              "text": ". This museum is not just a repository of artifacts; it’s a narrative of the ages, capturing the essence of Egypt’s diverse cultural and historical epochs. From the reign of the Pharaohs to the Greco-Roman influences, and from the Coptic era to Islamic times, the museum is a treasure trove for anyone fascinated by "
            },
            {
              "_key": "000000000004",
              "_type": "span",
              "marks": [
                "000000000003"
              ],
              "text": "Egypt’s multifaceted history"
            },
            {
              "_key": "000000000005",
              "_type": "span",
              "marks": [],
              "text": "."
            }
          ],
          "markDefs": [
            {
              "_key": "000000000003",
              "_pendingInternalRef": {
                "sourceLocale": "en",
                "wpUrl": "https://travel2egypt.org/the-worlds-first-labour-strike/"
              },
              "_type": "externalLink",
              "href": "/blog/kiroku-ni-nokoru-saiko-kyu-no-rodo-sutoraiki",
              "newTab": false
            },
            {
              "_key": "3eoenl5buc4c",
              "_type": "internalLink",
              "reference": {
                "_ref": "guideArticle.al-wadi-al-gadid.el-wadi-el-gedid-museum",
                "_type": "reference"
              }
            }
          ],
          "style": "normal"
        },
        {
          "_key": "000000000008",
          "_type": "block",
          "children": [
            {
              "_key": "000000000007",
              "_type": "span",
              "marks": [],
              "text": "Pharaonic Era Relics: "
            }
          ],
          "markDefs": [],
          "style": "h3"
        },
        {
          "_key": "00000000000d",
          "_type": "block",
          "children": [
            {
              "_key": "000000000009",
              "_type": "span",
              "marks": [],
              "text": "The museum’s significance is rooted in the strategic importance of the Al Wadi Al Gadid region during the time of the Pharaohs. It houses an impressive collection of artifacts from this era, including unique red-colored pots from the "
            },
            {
              "_key": "00000000000b",
              "_type": "span",
              "marks": [
                "00000000000a"
              ],
              "text": "Old Kingdom"
            },
            {
              "_key": "00000000000c",
              "_type": "span",
              "marks": [],
              "text": " and tools predating the dynastic periods. The museum also showcases portraits from local temples such as Hibis, Ndura, and Ghweita, offering glimpses into ancient life in the oases through various paintings and artifacts."
            }
          ],
          "markDefs": [
            {
              "_key": "00000000000a",
              "_type": "externalLink",
              "href": "https://www.ancient.eu/Old_Kingdom_of_Egypt/",
              "newTab": true
            }
          ],
          "style": "normal"
        },
        {
          "_key": "00000000000f",
          "_type": "block",
          "children": [
            {
              "_key": "00000000000e",
              "_type": "span",
              "marks": [],
              "text": "Greco-Roman Influences: "
            }
          ],
          "markDefs": [],
          "style": "h3"
        },
        {
          "_key": "00000000001a",
          "_type": "block",
          "children": [
            {
              "_key": "000000000010",
              "_type": "span",
              "marks": [],
              "text": "Al "
            },
            {
              "_key": "000000000012",
              "_type": "span",
              "marks": [
                "000000000011"
              ],
              "text": "Wadi Al Gadid’s"
            },
            {
              "_key": "000000000013",
              "_type": "span",
              "marks": [],
              "text": " strategic location along the Nile made it a focal point during the Roman conquest. The museum reflects this period through an array of "
            },
            {
              "_key": "000000000015",
              "_type": "span",
              "marks": [
                "000000000014"
              ],
              "text": "Greco-Roman"
            },
            {
              "_key": "000000000016",
              "_type": "span",
              "marks": [],
              "text": " artifacts, including jewelry made from precious stones, masks, coffins, and carved images of Amun, the predominant deity of that era. These objects illustrate the "
            },
            {
              "_key": "000000000018",
              "_type": "span",
              "marks": [
                "000000000017"
              ],
              "text": "cultural"
            },
            {
              "_key": "000000000019",
              "_type": "span",
              "marks": [],
              "text": " fusion and the impact of Roman governance in the region."
            }
          ],
          "markDefs": [
            {
              "_key": "000000000011",
              "_pendingInternalRef": {
                "sourceLocale": "en",
                "wpUrl": "https://travel2egypt.org/al-wadi-al-gadid-travel-guide/voyage-directions/"
              },
              "_type": "externalLink",
              "href": "/guide/al-wadi-al-gadid/how-to-go-in-al-wadi-al-gadid",
              "newTab": false
            },
            {
              "_key": "000000000014",
              "_pendingInternalRef": {
                "sourceLocale": "en",
                "wpUrl": "https://travel2egypt.org/alexandria-travel-guide/the-greco-roman-museum/"
              },
              "_type": "externalLink",
              "href": "/guide/alexandria/the-greco-roman-museum",
              "newTab": false
            },
            {
              "_key": "000000000017",
              "_pendingInternalRef": {
                "sourceLocale": "en",
                "wpUrl": "https://travel2egypt.org/animals-in-ancient-egypt/"
              },
              "_type": "externalLink",
              "href": "/blog/animales-en-el-antiguo-egipto",
              "newTab": false
            }
          ],
          "style": "normal"
        },
        {
          "_key": "00000000001c",
          "_type": "block",
          "children": [
            {
              "_key": "00000000001b",
              "_type": "span",
              "marks": [],
              "text": "Coptic and Islamic Artifacts: "
            }
          ],
          "markDefs": [],
          "style": "h3"
        },
        {
          "_key": "000000000027",
          "_type": "block",
          "children": [
            {
              "_key": "00000000001d",
              "_type": "span",
              "marks": [],
              "text": "The museum also tells the story of the Coptic Christians and Muslims in Al "
            },
            {
              "_key": "00000000001f",
              "_type": "span",
              "marks": [
                "00000000001e"
              ],
              "text": "Wadi Al Gadid"
            },
            {
              "_key": "000000000020",
              "_type": "span",
              "marks": [],
              "text": ". The "
            },
            {
              "_key": "000000000022",
              "_type": "span",
              "marks": [
                "000000000021"
              ],
              "text": "Coptic Christians"
            },
            {
              "_key": "000000000023",
              "_type": "span",
              "marks": [],
              "text": ", seeking refuge from Roman persecution, left behind sacred items like crosses of various materials, colorful portraits of saints, Jesus Christ, and the Virgin Mary, along with rare Coptic manuscripts. These artifacts provide insight into the early Christian era in "
            },
            {
              "_key": "000000000025",
              "_type": "span",
              "marks": [
                "000000000024"
              ],
              "text": "Egypt"
            },
            {
              "_key": "000000000026",
              "_type": "span",
              "marks": [],
              "text": "."
            }
          ],
          "markDefs": [
            {
              "_key": "00000000001e",
              "_pendingInternalRef": {
                "sourceLocale": "en",
                "wpUrl": "https://travel2egypt.org/al-wadi-al-gadid-travel-guide/activities-essential/"
              },
              "_type": "externalLink",
              "href": "https://travel2egypt.org/al-wadi-al-gadid-travel-guide/activities-essential/",
              "newTab": false
            },
            {
              "_key": "000000000021",
              "_pendingInternalRef": {
                "sourceLocale": "en",
                "wpUrl": "http://travel2egypt.org/cairo/coptic-cairo/"
              },
              "_type": "externalLink",
              "href": "/guide/cairo/coptic-cairo",
              "newTab": false
            },
            {
              "_key": "000000000024",
              "_pendingInternalRef": {
                "sourceLocale": "en",
                "wpUrl": "https://travel2egypt.org/al-arish-travel-guide/movement-guide/"
              },
              "_type": "externalLink",
              "href": "/guide/al-arish/getting-around-al-arish",
              "newTab": false
            }
          ],
          "style": "normal"
        },
        {
          "_key": "00000000002c",
          "_type": "block",
          "children": [
            {
              "_key": "000000000028",
              "_type": "span",
              "marks": [],
              "text": "In contrast, the Islamic influence is evident through artifacts from the "
            },
            {
              "_key": "00000000002a",
              "_type": "span",
              "marks": [
                "000000000029"
              ],
              "text": "period of Islamic occupation in Egypt"
            },
            {
              "_key": "00000000002b",
              "_type": "span",
              "marks": [],
              "text": ". The museum displays unique lamps used in mosques, inscriptions of Quranic verses on wood and paper, decorated pots, vessels, and weapons from the era. These items reflect the rich Islamic heritage and its integration into the fabric of Egyptian culture."
            }
          ],
          "markDefs": [
            {
              "_key": "000000000029",
              "_pendingInternalRef": {
                "sourceLocale": "en",
                "wpUrl": "https://travel2egypt.org/the-pyramids-of-egypt/"
              },
              "_type": "externalLink",
              "href": "/blog/ejiputo-no-piramiddo",
              "newTab": false
            }
          ],
          "style": "normal"
        },
        {
          "_key": "000000000034",
          "_type": "block",
          "children": [
            {
              "_key": "00000000002d",
              "_type": "span",
              "marks": [],
              "text": "The El Wadi El Gedid museum is more than a collection of artifacts; it’s a journey through time. It encapsulates the historical and "
            },
            {
              "_key": "00000000002f",
              "_type": "span",
              "marks": [
                "00000000002e"
              ],
              "text": "cultural evolution of Egypt"
            },
            {
              "_key": "000000000030",
              "_type": "span",
              "marks": [],
              "text": ", showcasing the confluence of civilizations that have shaped the region. For history enthusiasts and "
            },
            {
              "_key": "000000000032",
              "_type": "span",
              "marks": [
                "000000000031"
              ],
              "text": "cultural explorers, a visit to this museum is a voyage into the heart of Egypt’s storied past, revealing the layers of history that make Al Wadi Al Gadid a microcosm of Egypt’s"
            },
            {
              "_key": "000000000033",
              "_type": "span",
              "marks": [],
              "text": " grand historical narrative."
            }
          ],
          "markDefs": [
            {
              "_key": "00000000002e",
              "_pendingInternalRef": {
                "sourceLocale": "en",
                "wpUrl": "https://travel2egypt.org/faux-pas-to-avoid-in-egypt/"
              },
              "_type": "externalLink",
              "href": "/blog/ejiputo-de-shitsurei-ni-nara-nai-tame-ni",
              "newTab": false
            },
            {
              "_key": "000000000031",
              "_pendingInternalRef": {
                "sourceLocale": "en",
                "wpUrl": "https://travel2egypt.org/al-wadi-al-gadid-travel-guide/culinary-desert/"
              },
              "_type": "externalLink",
              "href": "/guide/al-wadi-al-gadid/food-in-al-wadi-al-gadid",
              "newTab": false
            }
          ],
          "style": "normal"
        },
        {
